	(text "# STORAGE MICROSD CARD SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (MICROSD BLOCK)\nProject: OpenMycoNet COMBO_NODE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 3.6\n\nSYSTEM OVERVIEW\nThe MicroSD card subsystem provides non-volatile data logging using a Hirose DM3AT push-push receptacle (J13) operating in 1-bit SPI bus mode. \nThe interface features a high-side load switch (U17 TPS22919) for power gating, controlled output discharge timing, hardware card detection, \npower decoupling, and SPI bus pull-up resistors.\n\n1. HIGH-SIDE POWER GATING LOAD SWITCH (U17 TPS22919DCKR)\n* Core IC: U17 (TPS22919DCKR ultra-low leakage load switch with Smart Quick Output Discharge).\n* Gated Supply Rail: Switches main +3.3V system input (decoupled by C44 10µF) to supply the SD card VDD rail (SD_VDD). \n  Eliminates 100 µA - 1 mA idle card current during sleep.\n* Control Line (SD_CARD_SLEEP): Driven by ESP32-S3 IO47 (shared with TPS3851 SET1 watchdog enable pin). Pulled LOW via 100kΩ resistor (R29) \n  on MCU sheet to keep power disabled by default.\n* Controlled Discharge Timing: External resistor R54 (1kΩ) connected between QOD (Pin 5) and SD_VDD (Pin 6), paired with C43 (47µF bulk capacitor), \n  enforces a controlled fall time (t_FALL ≈ 152 ms) upon turn-off to prevent supply bus glitches.\n\n2. CONNECTOR FOOTPRINT AND POWER DECOUPLING (J13 HIROSE DM3AT)\n* Memory Connector: J13 (Hirose DM3AT MicroSD receptacle with integrated mechanical card-detect switch).\n* VDD Power Rail: Pin 4 (VDD) connected directly to the switched SD_VDD rail from U17.\n* Local Decoupling: Filtered by C42 (100nF) and C43 (47µF) ceramic capacitors to handle peak card-write current spikes and maintain rail stability.\n* Grounding: Pin 6 (VSS) and outer metallic shield frame (SH) tied directly to system GND.\n\n3. SPI SIGNALING AND BUS PULL-UP NETWORK\n* Chip Select (SPI.SPI_CS): Pin 2 (DAT3/CD) acts as active-LOW chip select from ESP32-S3 (IO15); pulled HIGH to SD_VDD via R51 (10kΩ) \n  to prevent unselected floating states.\n* Master-Out Slave-In (SPI.SPI_MOSI): Pin 3 (CMD) receives data from ESP32-S3 (IO13); pulled HIGH to SD_VDD via R51 (10kΩ).\n* Serial Clock (SPI.SPI_SCK): Pin 5 (CLK) receives clock pulses from ESP32-S3 (IO14).\n* Master-In Slave-Out (SPI.SPI_MISO): Pin 7 (DAT0) outputs data to ESP32-S3 (IO12); pulled HIGH to SD_VDD via R52 (10kΩ).\n* Unused Data Lines: Pin 1 (DAT2) and Pin 8 (DAT1) pulled HIGH to SD_VDD via R48 (10kΩ) and R49 (10kΩ) per SD physical layer specs.\n* Leakage Prevention: All SPI GPIO lines configured to High-Z / Input mode prior to pulling SD_CARD_SLEEP LOW to prevent back-feeding \n  ESD protection diodes when SD_VDD is powered OFF.\n\n4. CARD DETECTION AND ACTIVITY INDICATOR\n* Card Detect Circuit (SPI.SD_DET): Pin 10 (DET_A) pulled HIGH to SD_VDD via R53 (10kΩ); Pin 9 (DET_B) tied to GND. \n  Inserting a card shorts DET_A to DET_B, pulling SPI.SD_DET LOW to signal insertion to ESP32-S3 (IO16).\n* Activity LED: Active-LOW LED D4 connected via R50 (1kΩ) between SD_VDD and SPI.SPI_CS line; illuminates during active SPI read/write cycles.\n\n5. SUBSYSTEM INTERFACE MATRIX\n* SW_EN_SD: High-side load switch enable input from ESP32-S3 (IO47), pulled LOW via R55 (100kΩ).\n* SPI.SPI_CS: Active-LOW Chip Select line connected to ESP32-S3 (IO15), pulled HIGH via R51 (10kΩ).\n* SPI.SPI_MOSI: SPI data input line connected to ESP32-S3 (IO13), pulled HIGH via R51 (10kΩ).\n* SPI.SPI_SCK: SPI clock input line driven by ESP32-S3 (IO14).\n* SPI.SPI_MISO: SPI data output line connected to ESP32-S3 (IO12), pulled HIGH via R52 (10kΩ).\n* SPI.SD_DET: Active-LOW mechanical card detect line connected to ESP32-S3 (IO16), pulled HIGH via R53 (10kΩ)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.462 62.738 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "bb937710-8f75-46de-9c8f-71567ddce723")
	)
